    "q-40425": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40425",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1}{{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{2}b \\\\  & =-4b \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
